body:
Hello,

I have the same problem: `Cannot read property 'directiveStart' of null` with since Angular 9.

The crash happens because [inside `ɵɵelementEnd()`](https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/416c786774dccc20d824737207be4e55cb53c9cc/packages/core/src/render3/instructions/element.ts#L131), `previousOrParentTNode.parent` is `null` (a type forcer `!` is added to override this case, but it happens to be `null` anyway).
Then, `registerPostOrderHooks()` is [called with `previousOrParentTNode = null`, which shoudn't happen and creates the crash](https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/416c786774dccc20d824737207be4e55cb53c9cc/packages/core/src/render3/hooks.ts#L74).

The following diff in `@angular/core` suppresses the crash, but results in some HTML tags being closed prematurely:
```diff
--- a/packages/core/src/render3/instructions/element.ts
+++ b/packages/core/src/render3/instructions/element.ts
@@ -126,6 +126,8 @@ export function ɵɵelementEnd(): void {
   ngDevMode && assertDefined(previousOrParentTNode, 'No parent node to close.');
   if (getIsParent()) {
     setIsNotParent();
+  } else if (!previousOrParentTNode.parent) {
+    return;
   } else {
     ngDevMode && assertHasParent(getPreviousOrParentTNode());
     previousOrParentTNode = previousOrParentTNode.parent !;
```

@benlesh I think you wrote that code in commit 5a724b3, do you have any hints so we can debug further?

Thanks in advance.
